---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy | Breezy Days OBX"
  description="How Breezy Days OBX uses information submitted with an availability request."
>
  <main class="policy-page" id="main-content">
    <article class="policy-card">
      <a class="wordmark" href="/#hero">Breezy Days <span>OBX</span></a>
      <p class="eyebrow">Prelaunch privacy notice</p>
      <h1>Privacy, in plain language.</h1>
      <p class="policy-updated">Last updated August 14, 2026</p>

      <h2>What an availability request includes</h2>
      <p>Arrival and departure dates, group size, and the email address where you want a reply.</p>

      <h2>Why we ask for it</h2>
      <p>
        These details are used to review the requested stay, reply about availability and fit,
        and explain the price and booking terms before you decide whether to reserve.
      </p>

      <h2>Processing and retention</h2>
      <p>
        The final form provider, storage location, retention period, and deletion process will be
        named here before public inquiries open. Breezy Days does not sell availability-request
        information.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions about your information</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:breezydaysobx@gmail.com">breezydaysobx@gmail.com</a> to ask what was
        submitted or request deletion, subject to any recordkeeping obligations that apply.
      </p>

      <p class="policy-status">
        This notice is part of the local prelaunch build and must be finalized with the owner after
        the form provider and operating workflow are configured.
      </p>
      <a class="button" href="/#availability">Back to availability</a>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

